# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# iCloud
#
# ~/Documents is synced by "Desktop & Documents Folders", and iCloud loses races
# against directories that churn: it forked `.git/index` fifteen times and
# `.git/refs/heads/main` twice in a single afternoon, which is enough to break
# `git fetch` outright ("fatal: bad object refs/heads/main 2"). It has done the
# same to `.next` and, in the past, to source files — a stray `page 2.tsx` makes
# tsc fail with duplicate identifiers.
#
# iCloud skips anything whose name ends in `.nosync`, so the three churning
# directories live under that suffix and are symlinked back to their real names.
# These entries exist because git ignores `.git` by that exact name and would
# otherwise offer to commit the entire repository into itself.
/.git.nosync
/.next.nosync
/node_modules.nosync

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Secrets: ignore every .env variant, but the placeholder template must be committed
!.env.example

# Local Postgres / tooling
/coverage
/playwright-report
/test-results

# Local editor/tooling config
/.claude

# Development email capture and local object storage (never committed)
/.mail
/.storage
